| Crisp paper: one cool ground and one sans for reading on every client, cool rules, the code's own inks in a well; the type sizes unchanged (2026-10-05) | #326 | **has** | Walked 2026-10-05 on `/tmp/run-crispy326` with one session (*Repo notes*: an ask, a read of `NOTES.md`, a reply with a Swift snippet). The page in headless Chrome at 1440 × 900, light and dark, with `prefers-color-scheme` emulated, and the window by window id over AX in each appearance. Read off the page: `--paper-ground` #f7f8f9 over #1c1d20, `--paper-sidebar` #f0f1f3 over #161719, `--paper-well` #f0f2f4 over #2a2d31, `--paper-rule` and `--paper-selection` #dde1e6 over #3a3e44, `--paper-ink` #1c1d20 over #e8eaed, `--accent` #5b3be0 over #ab8eff (cobalt #1f5fc8 over #7fb0ff since #695); a turn computed to the system sans at 15 px (`--font-text`) and a snippet to `ui-monospace` at 12 px on the well, and no serif in the chat, the sidebar or the body — before, the page's turn was the system serif at 15 px (#148). Every ink clears 4.5:1 on the ground and in the well; accent on the dark selection is 4.12:1 and no accent text is drawn there. Shots and readings: `walks/326/` (`page-{light,dark,dark-steps}.png`, `window-{light,dark}.png`, `notes.txt`). The window's own `Paper.swift` is the page's `theme/paper.css`, one file's values in the other's language, so a row that changes a row here changes a row there. |
